## Why This Is Asked
Tests endianness understanding and safe 128-bit lane manipulation with pure bitwise ops.

## Key Concepts
- Byte reversal with masks
- 128-bit struct arithmetic
- Endianness swapping

## Code Example
```javascript
static inline uint64_t reverseBytes64(uint64_t x){
  x = ((x & 0x00FF00FF00FF00FFULL) << 8) | ((x >> 8) & 0x00FF00FF00FF00FFULL);
  x = ((x & 0x0000FFFF0000FFFFULL) << 16) | ((x >> 16) & 0x0000FFFF0000FFFFULL);
  x = (x << 32) | (x >> 32);
  return x;
}

uint128 swapEndian128(uint128 x){
  uint128 r;
  r.hi = reverseBytes64(x.lo);
  r.lo = reverseBytes64(x.hi);
  return r;
}
```

